  "construction": "Surface code of the orientably-regular map C163.13 of type {8,8} (genus 163) in M. Conder's list of chiral maps of genus 2 to 301. Rotation group G = <r,s | r^8, s^8, (r*s)^2, s^-1*r^-1*s^2*r^3*s^2*r^-1*s^-1*r, s^-1*r^-1*s*r*s^-1*r^2*s^-1*r*s^-2*r> of order 1296. Darts = elements of G (right multiplication), faces = cosets g<r>, vertices = cosets g<s>, edges = cosets g<rs> = {g, grs}. Qubits on the 648 edges, X-checks on the 162 vertices (weight 8), Z-checks on the 162 faces (weight 8), incidences mod 2: H_X and H_Z are the boundary maps of the cellular chain complex over F_2, k = 2 - chi = 326, d_Z is the shortest homologically nontrivial cycle of the map and d_X that of the dual map. Found in a census of regular maps (normal subgroups of the triangle groups <r,s | r^p, s^q, (rs)^2>, Magma's LowIndexNormalSubgroups). The qubit order is that of the dart permutations in the public package in the references (data/maps.json), whose src/rebuild.py rebuilds these matrices from them and from the presentation.",
